---
import SwitchCase from "@/components/ui/display/SwitchCase.astro";
import type { TransferableSkillMeta } from "@/utils/transferableSkills";

export const meta: TransferableSkillMeta = {
	title: "Sales and Business development",
	summary: "Self-employed mastery of B2B/B2C sales - 90%+ revenue from referrals; scaled to 160+ projects via freelancers.",
	icon: "ph:handshake-duotone",
	featured: true,
	order: 10,
	keywords: ["sales", "business-development", "b2b", "b2c", "referrals", "freelance"],
};

interface Props {
	only?: string;
}
const { only } = Astro.props;
---

<SwitchCase value={only}>
	<Fragment slot="card">
		<p>
			Being self-employed has required mastering sales, both in B2C and B2B contexts, to sustain and grow my business. From 2010 to 2014, as a personal coach, I balanced emotion and logic to
			demonstrate the value of my services without a clear ROI. Since 2014, freelancing as a developer shifted my focus to understanding business needs and delivering tailored solutions, such as
			websites, e-commerce stores, or SaaS platforms, that provided measurable ROI. Exceptional customer service and quality work have led to over 90% of my sales coming through referrals and
			repeat business. As demand grew, I scaled by hiring freelancers, managing and delegating work to complete over 160 projects between 2014 and 2019, and many more since.
		</p>
	</Fragment>

	<Fragment slot="default">
		<p>
			Freelancing and being self-employed has meant that sales aptitude has been critical to remaining in business. Sure... I could have outsourced it in order to drive business in, but such a
			core part of the business should never be outsourced.
		</p>

		<p>
			From 2010 to 2014, whilst personal coaching, <strong>B2C sales was required</strong>, understanding how my service could help on the prospect in their personal life. This meant there was
			not always a clear quantitative ROI, and it was based on how much value they would receive. This meant needing to balance emotion and logic in order to reach a successful sale.
		</p>

		<p>
			Since 2014, while freelancing as a developer, this <strong>shifted to B2B sales</strong>. Understanding what was needed within the prospects business, and connecting that to the solution
			that would deliver a specific ROI for them. Many times this was a simple website, an e-commerce store or creating a SaaS platform; and it was a prerequisite to discover not only what was
			important to them (e.g., analytics for certain stages of their sales funnel), but also deliver a solution that was competitively priced but didn't compromise on the quality.
		</p>

		<p class="my-10 text-lg font-semibold">
			After delivering a quality product and giving great customer service, I found that more and more business came to me through word-of-mouth referrals from satisfied clients who came to know
			me as a trusted advisor and passed on my details to colleagues and friends. In fact, <strong
				>over 90% of the sales I have made, have been from word-of-mouth and repeat business from existing customers</strong
			>.
		</p>

		<p>
			As more customers and larger projects came my way, I was in need of help... I was running out of time to do everything. From here I hired freelancers to sub-contract some of the work to,
			needing me to manage and delegate work to them. This of course, came with its own challenges but doing so allowed me to take on more and bigger projects <strong
				>completing over 160 projects from 2014 - 2019</strong
			> and many more since.
		</p>
	</Fragment>
</SwitchCase>
